# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore — Smilers Chat Mobile
#
# Purpose: drastically reduce the Cloud Build context size shipped to the
# Emergent deployment pipeline. Without this file, EVERY commit shipped
# 650MB+ of Expo node_modules + cached build artifacts into the
# `COPY . /app` step, causing slow push, oversized layer rejections at
# the registry ("manifest invalid: Request contains an invalid argument"
# observed 2026-06-05), and leaking a server-side Firebase Admin SDK
# private key into the container image.
#
# After this file lands, build context drops to a few MB and pushes
# become reliable.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1) Node / Expo / Metro
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 641MB of frontend deps — installed inside the container, never copied
# from host. The backend container doesn't need them at all (FastAPI
# service); the frontend is built/served via EAS, not this image.
**/node_modules/
**/.npm/
**/.yarn/cache/
**/.yarn/install-state.gz
**/.pnp/
**/.pnp.js

# Expo development caches
**/.expo/
**/.expo-shared/
**/metro-cache/
**/.metro-cache/

# Built web bundle output (regenerated at deploy time if needed)
frontend/dist/
frontend/dist-android-check/
frontend/web-build/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2) Sensitive credentials
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Firebase Admin SDK service-account key — server-side Firebase
# credentials. Already uploaded to Expo's push credentials section
# (https://expo.dev/accounts/abcsimplesend/projects/smilers/credentials)
# so it's NOT needed in the deployed container. Including it would
# leak a private key with full Firebase project authority.
frontend/google-service-account.json
**/google-service-account*.json

# Test/dev credentials (already in .gitignore but belt-and-suspenders)
memory/test_credentials.md
memory/test_credentials*.md

# Generic key/secret/cert file patterns
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.p8
*.keystore
credentials.json
token.json

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3) Version control / IDE / OS / docs
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Markdown docs — except the contract doc which is intentionally
# shipped so backend agent can read it from any deployment.
README.md
**/CHANGELOG.md

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4) Python build artifacts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/venv/
**/.venv/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5) Logs / temp / scratch
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
dump.rdb
**/tmp/
**/.tmp/

# Large archive blobs (any zip/tar in the tree is almost certainly a
# build artifact, not a source file)
**/*.zip
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.tar
**/*.tgz
**/*.pack
**/*.deb
**/*.dylib

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6) Local-only Android SDK / Gradle (for `expo prebuild` users)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
frontend/android/
frontend/ios/
**/android-sdk/
**/.gradle/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7) Test / coverage outputs
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/coverage/
**/.nyc_output/
**/junit.xml
test_result.md

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Explicit ALLOW (overrides the rules above)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# We DO need the public Firebase client config (NOT a secret — it's
# embedded in every Android APK and is meant to be public per Google
# docs). Don't let the wildcard above accidentally exclude it.
!frontend/google-services.json

# Allow .env files — Emergent deployment pipeline reads these for
# runtime configuration (backend MONGO_URL, frontend EXPO_PUBLIC_*).
!**/.env
